      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Spontaneous coronary artery dissection is an uncommon clinical entity, its presentation and management similar to atherosclerotic coronary artery disease. We report on a young adult male who presented with myocardial infarction due to simultaneous dissection of left anterior descending and right coronary artery. He was treated with bilateral interal mammary artery grafts."},
